                    // signed (INT). Measured per operator on one source, only
                    // the operator changed: `*` `/` `-` reduce to INT, `+` and
                    // `<<` to UINT — in every declaration form (untyped,
                    // `int`, `bit [7:0]`).
                    // ...and the signedness PROPAGATES UP THROUGH `+`: Surelog
